title ALES113 — Lotus's move, relocate a span in place (the relocate-twin of duplicate)
prompt recur the itinerary Lindy-first crux-first; after ALES112 sent, take the next agent-doable Lotus lap, self-approve, prove GREEN, send as its own signed round; STOP at custody gates
think ALES112's duplicate COPIES a span (the clip grows). The other gesture a keeper reaches for when a bar is in the wrong place is move: lift the span out of one spot and land it at another, the clip's length HOLDING. Circle a bar, drag it — the verse pulled ahead of the chorus, the stray breath slid to a rest, the loop nudged whole to a new beat. Naming it beside duplicate completes the copy/relocate pair on a selection: repeat it where it is, or carry it somewhere new. Universal DAW gesture, Lindy-durable, absent from the suite (checked: no move.rye).
think Shape: move(clip, start, count, dest) copies the span [start, start+count) into one bounded scratch buffer (max_clip = 4*1024 = 4096, the same budget the Clip's own buffer names), then ALES2's cut removes it in place (the clip shrinks by count) and ALES2's splice reinserts the saved span at dest (the clip grows back by count) — the net length unchanged, no third primitive invented. dest names a position in the timeline AFTER the span is removed (0 <= dest <= len - count); because the head [0, start) has length start, dest = start is the identity and the inverse is exactly move(dest, count, start). Composing the two proven primitives means splice can never refuse ClipFull here (net length unchanged), and every range is refused BadRange before any write.
think Four laws: the MOVE law (the clip is the removed timeline with the span reinserted at dest, proven forward, backward, and to the head); the INVERSE law — the crux tying it to ALES2's cut and splice: move(start,count,dest) then move(dest,count,start) returns the original byte for byte, move its own inverse under swapped endpoints; the PRESERVATION / PEAK law (move relocates existing samples and invents none, the length unchanged and the multiset unchanged, so the peak re-measured through ALES13 is unchanged); the DEGENERATE / REFUSAL law (count 0 the identity, dest = start the identity, a start past the samples or a count past the remainder or a dest past len - count each BadRange, before any write).
obs Witness GREEN on the first pass — all four laws, all three BadRange branches (bad start, bad count, bad dest), and both identities (count 0, dest = start). Choosing post-removal coordinates for dest is what keeps the law crisp: the identity is a clean dest = start and the inverse is the same op with endpoints swapped, so relocate reads as a matched pair the way cut/splice already compose. Standing on cut + splice rather than open-coding the shuffle means the bounds live in ONE place and the net-length-unchanged fact makes ClipFull unreachable. TAME style bans clean (ratchet zero-assert count unchanged); >=2 positive-invariant asserts per fn; width-check clean; the one bounded scratch buffer names its max; timeline.EditError reused whole. No custody gate touched — pure-Rye local i16 buffer, siloed to lotus/.
